# CS611-Assignment 1
## Sliding Game
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Name: Ian Ding
- Email: iding918@bu.edu
- Student ID: U66239752


## Files
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runner.java: This is a wrapper that is used to create an instance of our game and start it.
Game.java: This class handles reading and writing to and from the terminal for the game. It also controls the main game loop.
Board.java: This class implements the board object. It handles the maintence of the game state including verifying a win, finding legal moves, making slides, and setting up the 
            game board. 


## Notes
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. All of the scrambles are solvable because they are generated how a board would be shuffled in real life. With a random number of random slides.
2. Map can be extended to 3-D

## How to compile and run
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Navigate to the directory "Sliding Game" after unzipping the files
2. Run the following instructions:
javac *.java
java Runner

